  message: "FYI from the mulul run (branch jgstern-agent/fix/mulul-catalogue-rows, local, commit e94b1aace0), bearing on INV-dukam's remaining half: go.yaml's os/exec row is now [Command, CommandContext] (LookPath moved to fs_read) and carries a note saying the two stay subprocess until taint is represented through the *Cmd receiver into Run/Start/Output (ADR-0049 ruling 3) -- citing this item. The community go-x-sys-and-grpc.yaml execabs row is likewise [Command, CommandContext]. test_go_lookpath_is_not_a_launch.py::test_control_the_constructors_are_untouched_pending_wi_kozaj pins both modules' Command/CommandContext as subprocess; the stage-4 change that removes them should update that control. Expect a textual conflict on that go.yaml row if both branches edit it."  # a961
- op: discuss  # b393
  at: '2026-10-03T14:46:07Z'  # b393
  by: agent  # b393
  actor: jgstern_agent  # b393
  clock: 5  # b393
  nonce: b393  # b393
  message: "WORK DONE 2026-10-03 (decontend run, stage 2). Branch jgstern-agent/fix/kozaj (local, not pushed), two commits on origin/dev e58250d713:\n  12324da54b fix(catalogue): row the csv.DictWriter write surface\n  00d8e93be1 fix(python): type a library factory's result from its signature row; move the csv.writer row to the executor\nPART 1: python.yaml rows csv.DictWriter [writerow, writerows, writeheader] fs_write (methods, ADR-0059); the csv completeness note enumerates the public surface; community mirror defusedcsv.csv.DictWriter; CATALOGUE_SCOPE admits csv.DictWriter. No analyzer change: the instance was already typed.\nPART 2 (the general mechanism): py.py _library_producer_type types the result of a call whose IMPORT-RESOLVED qualified callee is a key in library_signatures (built-in, community, user channel; read at call time), at the existing seam _external_constructor_type, so assignment, chain root, with-item, self field and call-site argument all use it. Declared rows go before the PascalCase convention. A from-imported owner (from defusedcsv import csv; csv.writer(f)) resolves too, for declared types only. Rows: csv.writer -> _csv.Writer; _csv.Writer [writerow, writerows] fs_write; the csv.writer fs_write row REMOVED (ADR-0049 Ruling 3; the csv slot's completeness entry keeps the factory call examined). Community mirror: library_signatures/python-stdlib-dropins.yaml defusedcsv.csv.writer -> defusedcsv.csv._ProxyWriter (surface read from raphaelm/defusedcsv csv.py), _ProxyWriter rows, defusedcsv.csv writer row removed. Reuse: add `<qualified producer>: <type>` + an executor row; no analyzer change (WI-dibit's build_opener verified through the user channel in a test).\nFIXTURES, verify-claims host_secret -> host_fs (dev e58250d713 / part 1 / part 2):\n  same-scope csv.writer(f).writerow: violated at csv.writer (ddg_mixed, approximate) / same / violated at _csv.Writer.writerow (precise)\n  DictWriter: inconclusive \"could not classify (csv.DictWriter)\" / violated at csv.DictWriter.writeheader + writerow / same\n  writer built in caller, written in callee: confirmed_with_caveats (FALSE CLEAN) / same / violated at _csv.Writer.writerow\n  from csv import writer; writer(f).writerows: violated at csv.writer / same / violated at _csv.Writer.writerows\n  clean writer (no secret): confirmed_with_caveats (untyped writerow) at part 1 / confirmed at part 2\n  from defusedcsv import csv: violated at defusedcsv.csv.writer (approximate) at part 1 / violated at _ProxyWriter.writerow (precise, plus the DictWriter flow) at part 2\nio-boundaries fs_write primitives: dev writer=[csv.writer], DictWriter=[]; part 2 writer=[_csv.Writer.writerow], DictWriter=[csv.DictWriter.writeheader, csv.DictWriter.writerow].\nCORPUS A/B (part 1 vs part 2, generic-taint-claims.yaml, 7 claims): pretix, sherpa-onnx, whisper.cpp, transformers. 28 of 28 verdicts and every flow count unchanged. One flow relocated on sherpa-onnx (scripts/whisper/tools/whisper_timestamps_csv.py main, argv -> csv.writer becomes argv -> _csv.Writer.writerow, same ddg_mixed method). 0 flows lost. Edge-level control on pretix's 4 csv-writing files: part 1 = 7 factory sites classified + 10 untyped writerow; part 2 = 10 typed writerow classified (2 _csv.Writer, 8 defusedcsv _ProxyWriter), 0 untyped. Edge-level control NOT run on whisper.cpp / transformers. Arms printed their code-under-test trees (armA / armB snapshots).\nTESTS: part 1 smart-test 9872 passed, 2 failed (a CATALOGUE_SCOPE entry, fixed; a hypothesis too_slow health check in tests/test_transcript_pipeline_properties.py, unrelated), rerun of both files + new test 655 passed. Part 2 smart-test (519 files, py.py at 100% scoped coverage) 15430 passed, 1 failed (a defusedcsv community test, fixed), rerun 48 passed. New tests red first: 10 failed on part 1's file before the rows, 8 failed on the producer file before the py.py change; the from-import convention control was mutation-checked.\nRESIDUAL FILED: WI-munab (writes into an in-memory io.StringIO classify fs_write; pretix vouchers.py:116, waitinglist.py:322). Notes posted on WI-dibit, INV-dukam, WI-jidij."  # b393
