  message: "Merged in PR #1417 (dev c5249c1aa1).\n\nFixed on the filed instance (branch jgstern-agent/fix/kozaj, 12324da54b + 00d8e93be1). Defect 1: csv.DictWriter [writerow, writerows, writeheader] rowed fs_write; repro `dw = csv.DictWriter(f, ...); dw.writerow({\"a\": os.environ[\"API_KEY\"]})` with host_secret -> host_fs went inconclusive (\"could not classify (csv.DictWriter)\") -> violated at csv.DictWriter.writerow (test_csv_write_surface.py::TestTheFindingIsReported, production CLI path). Defect 2: `csv.writer: _csv.Writer` declared in library_signatures and consumed by the new general py.py producer lookup; `_csv.Writer.writerow/writerows` rowed; the constructor row removed under Ruling 3. Repro `def dump(w): w.writerow([secret])` / `w = csv.writer(f); dump(w)` went confirmed_with_caveats -> violated at _csv.Writer.writerow (TestTheWriterFindingSurvivesTheMove::...through-a-parameter). Corpus A/B on 4 repos: no verdict or flow count moved, 1 flow relocated to the executor, 0 lost. Not asserted: that every python factory is typed (only rowed ones are); member-return rows on typed receivers remain unconsumed."  # 0664
